<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;CEDERCREUTZ FAMILY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Cedercreutz Family is a Swedish-Finnish noble family with a rich history spanning centuries, known for their contributions to Finnish heritage and culture."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ERIK CEDERCREUTZ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Erik Cedercreutz is the patriarch of the Cedercreutz family, known for his administrative skills and appointment as the Governor of Vyborg."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOHAN CEDERCREUTZ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Johan Cedercreutz is the son of Erik and a military strategist who defended Finland against Russian invasions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARL CEDERCREUTZ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carl Cedercreutz is the son of Johan and a prominent figure in the Finnish War of 1808-1809."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VYBORG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vyborg is a strategic province in eastern Finland where Erik Cedercreutz served as the Governor."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PORVOO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Porvoo is the picturesque town where the Cedercreutz family's estate was located, serving as a hub of cultural activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SWEDEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sweden is mentioned as the former ruler of Finland during the 16th century when the Cedercreutz family first rose to prominence."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUSSIAN EMPIRE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Russian Empire is referenced as the adversary that the Cedercreutz family defended against."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Finland is the primary setting of the Cedercreutz family's influence and contributions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SWEDISH MONARCHY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Swedish Monarchy is mentioned as the authority that appointed Erik Cedercreutz as the Governor of Vyborg."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINNISH WAR OF 1808-1809&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Finnish War of 1808-1809 is an event where Carl Cedercreutz fought against the Russian occupation."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOURNAL OF NORDIC GENEALOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Journal of Nordic Genealogy is a publication that published a study re-examining the origins of the Cedercreutz family."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANADIAN JOURNAL OF ARCHAEOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Canadian Journal of Archaeology is a publication that published a study on archaeological findings related to the Cedercreutz family."&lt;SEP&gt;"Canadian Journal of Archaeology is the publication where the paper by Bélanger on the Cedercreutz Settlement was published."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FINNISH HISTORICAL SOCIETY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Finnish Historical Society is a publication that published a study on the early history of the Cedercreutz family in Finland."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUEBEC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Quebec is the location where the earliest recorded ancestor of the Cedercreutz family is believed to have emigrated from."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SWEDEN OR FINLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sweden or Finland are locations that were previously assumed to be the origin of the Cedercreutz family."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CANADA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Canada is the location where recent research suggests the Cedercreutz family's origins can be traced back to."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;16TH CENTURY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 16th century marks the period when the Cedercreutz family first rose to prominence in Finland."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;17TH CENTURY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 17th century marks the period when Erik Cedercreutz arrived in Finland and established himself as a prominent merchant and landowner."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1650&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1650 is the year when the Cedercreutz family earned a noble title."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AURORA BOREALIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aurora Borealis is mentioned as dancing across the night sky in Northern Europe."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOBLE FAMILY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Cedercreutz family is described as a noble family with a rich history spanning centuries."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRATEGIC PROVINCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vyborg is referred to as a strategic province in eastern Finland."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRATEGIC SETTLEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Cedercreutz family's early settlement in Quebec is described as a strategic settlement."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRATEGIC POSITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Cedercreutz family's position in Vyborg is described as strategic."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARCHAEOLOGICAL FINDINGS AT THE CEDERCREUTZ SETTLEMENT, QUEBEC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This event involves archaeological findings at the Cedercreutz Settlement in Quebec, providing insights into the area's past."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BÉLANGER, P.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"P. Bélanger is the author of a paper on archaeological findings at the Cedercreutz Settlement, Quebec."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CEDERCREUTZ SETTLEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cedercreutz Settlement is the site of archaeological findings discussed in the paper."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KNUUTILA, J.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"J. Knuutila is mentioned as another author, though no specific work is detailed in the given text."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0181</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;CANADIAN JOURNAL OF ARCHAEOLOGY&quot;" target="&quot;ARCHAEOLOGICAL FINDINGS AT THE CEDERCREUTZ SETTLEMENT, QUEBEC&quot;">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The paper on the archaeological findings at the Cedercreutz Settlement, Quebec was published in the Canadian Journal of Archaeology."</data>
      <data key="d5">"publication, academic contribution"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0181</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ARCHAEOLOGICAL FINDINGS AT THE CEDERCREUTZ SETTLEMENT, QUEBEC&quot;" target="&quot;BÉLANGER, P.&quot;">
      <data key="d3">18.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"P. Bélanger authored a paper on the archaeological findings at the Cedercreutz Settlement, Quebec."</data>
      <data key="d5">"authorship, research"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0181</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ARCHAEOLOGICAL FINDINGS AT THE CEDERCREUTZ SETTLEMENT, QUEBEC&quot;" target="&quot;KNUUTILA, J.&quot;">
      <data key="d3">5.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"J. Knuutila is mentioned as another author, though no specific relationship is detailed in the given text."</data>
      <data key="d5">"co-authorship, unspecified role"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0181</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
